{"videoId":"nTnYSzjfvqU","source":"auto","lang":"en","sentences":[{"start":0.0,"end":2.72,"text":"How good is your English pronunciation?"},{"start":2.72,"end":4.36,"text":"Let's find out."},{"start":4.36,"end":6.08,"text":"I will give you a pronunciation"},{"start":6.08,"end":8.6,"text":"test that will test your ability"},{"start":8.6,"end":10.52,"text":"to hear and to pronounce"},{"start":10.52,"end":14.44,"text":"vowel sounds. I'm also going to teach you how to produce"},{"start":14.44,"end":15.64,"text":"some of the trickiest"},{"start":15.64,"end":19.76,"text":"vowel sounds that even advanced speakers often mispronounce."},{"start":19.76,"end":22.84,"text":"Most English classes don't teach pronunciation"},{"start":22.84,"end":23.8,"text":"in detail."},{"start":23.8,"end":27.52,"text":"So, today we're going to work on both your listening skills"},{"start":27.52,"end":29.08,"text":"and your pronunciation."},{"start":29.08,"end":32.88,"text":"Keep track of your score and let me know how many mistakes you made. And if"},{"start":32.88,"end":36.32,"text":"you would like to truly master English pronunciation,"},{"start":36.32,"end":37.92,"text":"at the end of this video,"},{"start":37.92,"end":43.84,"text":"I will tell you more about my American accent training options, including how you can receive"},{"start":43.84,"end":44.56,"text":"regular"},{"start":44.56,"end":45.48,"text":"personalized"},{"start":45.48,"end":47.2,"text":"feedback on your accent"},{"start":47.2,"end":50.36,"text":"from me and one of my expert instructors"},{"start":50.36,"end":52.24,"text":"without paying for expensive"},{"start":52.24,"end":54.0,"text":"one-on-one training."},{"start":54.0,"end":57.44,"text":"All right, let's get started. Let's look at the first question."},{"start":57.44,"end":62.2,"text":"Which word contains a vowel sound that is different from the others?"},{"start":62.2,"end":65.04,"text":"Or, are they all the same?"},{"start":65.04,"end":68.24,"text":"What do you think?"},{"start":68.24,"end":70.92,"text":"The correct answer is foot."},{"start":70.92,"end":73.32,"text":"Listen to my pronunciation."},{"start":73.32,"end":74.52,"text":"food"},{"start":74.52,"end":75.68,"text":"foot"},{"start":75.68,"end":77.08,"text":"mood"},{"start":77.08,"end":78.04,"text":"moon"},{"start":78.04,"end":80.76,"text":"The double O spelling can be confusing."},{"start":80.76,"end":85.16,"text":"Sometimes it's pronounced as an oo sound, as in too,"},{"start":85.16,"end":86.24,"text":"cool,"},{"start":86.24,"end":87.64,"text":"or food."},{"start":87.64,"end":90.68,"text":"You probably have the same sound in your language."},{"start":90.68,"end":94.72,"text":"But, sometimes the double O is pronounced as an uh sound."},{"start":94.72,"end":97.12,"text":"Uh, as in foot,"},{"start":97.12,"end":98.44,"text":"book,"},{"start":98.44,"end":99.76,"text":"should."},{"start":99.76,"end":101.68,"text":"Look at the shape of my mouth."},{"start":101.68,"end":107.16,"text":"For the oo sound, my lips are pushed forward. Oo, oo. And the uh sound is"},{"start":107.16,"end":110.8,"text":"called a neutral vowel sound. The tongue is relaxed"},{"start":110.8,"end":114.4,"text":"and the lips are a little bit farther down in the back. Uh."},{"start":114.4,"end":119.12,"text":"Uh. And the lips are not very rounded at all. So, let's compare."},{"start":119.12,"end":120.04,"text":"Ooh."},{"start":120.04,"end":121.44,"text":"food"},{"start":121.44,"end":122.24,"text":"uh"},{"start":122.24,"end":123.84,"text":"uh foot"},{"start":123.84,"end":125.48,"text":"book"},{"start":125.48,"end":126.64,"text":"should"},{"start":126.64,"end":128.8,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":128.8,"end":132.52,"text":"Which vowel sound is different in these four words?"},{"start":132.52,"end":137.24,"text":"You say them."},{"start":137.24,"end":139.08,"text":"The first word is different."},{"start":139.08,"end":140.08,"text":"Listen."},{"start":140.08,"end":141.56,"text":"comma"},{"start":141.56,"end":143.0,"text":"coma"},{"start":143.0,"end":144.8,"text":"comb"},{"start":144.8,"end":146.16,"text":"don't"},{"start":146.16,"end":147.84,"text":"A comma is a punctuation"},{"start":147.84,"end":148.68,"text":"mark."},{"start":148.68,"end":151.4,"text":"Don't forget to add the comma."},{"start":151.4,"end":152.52,"text":"And a coma"},{"start":152.52,"end":154.16,"text":"is a medical state."},{"start":154.16,"end":157.0,"text":"The patient is in a coma."},{"start":157.0,"end":158.36,"text":"Did you get those correct?"},{"start":158.36,"end":163.44,"text":"Let's look at the next one. Which vowel sound is pronounced differently in these words?"},{"start":163.44,"end":165.2,"text":"Or are they all the same?"},{"start":165.2,"end":169.08,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":169.08,"end":170.92,"text":"They're all the same."},{"start":170.92,"end":173.72,"text":"Does that surprise you? Listen."},{"start":173.72,"end":174.92,"text":"hurt"},{"start":174.92,"end":176.28,"text":"learn"},{"start":176.28,"end":177.64,"text":"bird"},{"start":177.64,"end":179.04,"text":"world"},{"start":179.04,"end":181.92,"text":"That last one is commonly mispronounced."},{"start":181.92,"end":183.0,"text":"World."},{"start":183.0,"end":188.8,"text":"Some common words spelled with w o r are pronounced as er"},{"start":188.8,"end":189.64,"text":"er."},{"start":189.64,"end":191.08,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":191.08,"end":192.64,"text":"work"},{"start":192.64,"end":194.48,"text":"worth"},{"start":194.48,"end":196.56,"text":"word"},{"start":196.56,"end":198.36,"text":"worm"},{"start":198.36,"end":199.92,"text":"world"},{"start":199.92,"end":203.16,"text":"Repeat after me. I work for a worldwide"},{"start":203.16,"end":206.64,"text":"company."},{"start":206.64,"end":208.84,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":208.84,"end":213.04,"text":"Which word is pronounced with a different vowel sound from the rest?"},{"start":213.04,"end":218.08,"text":"Or are they all the same?"},{"start":218.08,"end":219.64,"text":"They're all the same."},{"start":219.64,"end":222.92,"text":"All four words have the same vowel sound."},{"start":222.92,"end":225.2,"text":"Let's practice. Repeat after me."},{"start":225.2,"end":227.04,"text":"cookie"},{"start":227.04,"end":228.56,"text":"look"},{"start":228.56,"end":230.04,"text":"put"},{"start":230.04,"end":231.64,"text":"wool"},{"start":231.64,"end":234.72,"text":"Wool is the trickiest one because the W"},{"start":234.72,"end":239.64,"text":"requires you to round your lips. Wuh wuh, but then you have to pull them back"},{"start":239.64,"end":242.64,"text":"pretty quickly to get into the uh position."},{"start":242.64,"end":244.96,"text":"Otherwise, it'll sound like wool."},{"start":244.96,"end":247.12,"text":"So, it's going to be like this. Wool."},{"start":247.12,"end":248.08,"text":"Wool."},{"start":248.08,"end":249.92,"text":"You say it."},{"start":249.92,"end":251.4,"text":"wool"},{"start":251.4,"end":254.2,"text":"I love your wool sweater."},{"start":254.2,"end":255.2,"text":"wool"},{"start":255.2,"end":257.44,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":257.44,"end":261.56,"text":"Which word has a different vowel sound from the rest?"},{"start":261.56,"end":265.48,"text":"Or are they all the same?"},{"start":265.48,"end":268.2,"text":"The correct answer is pool."},{"start":268.2,"end":271.16,"text":"The last one is pronounced differently from the rest."},{"start":271.16,"end":274.36,"text":"Repeat after me. wood"},{"start":274.36,"end":275.92,"text":"should"},{"start":275.92,"end":277.2,"text":"look"},{"start":277.2,"end":278.8,"text":"pool"},{"start":278.8,"end":280.4,"text":"Did you get that one right?"},{"start":280.4,"end":286.56,"text":"And by the way, would, could, and should are all pronounced with the same neutral vowel"},{"start":286.56,"end":288.64,"text":"sound, the uh sound."},{"start":288.64,"end":290.28,"text":"That's a common mistake."},{"start":290.28,"end":294.48,"text":"Repeat after me. I would if I could."},{"start":294.48,"end":296.8,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":296.8,"end":302.4,"text":"Which word is pronounced with a different vowel sound from the rest?"},{"start":302.4,"end":305.12,"text":"Or are they all pronounced the same?"},{"start":305.12,"end":307.6,"text":"The correct answer is cost."},{"start":307.6,"end":309.6,"text":"Listen to my pronunciation."},{"start":309.6,"end":311.04,"text":"most"},{"start":311.04,"end":312.44,"text":"post"},{"start":312.44,"end":314.2,"text":"cost"},{"start":314.2,"end":315.48,"text":"toast"},{"start":315.48,"end":319.12,"text":"Did you get that one right? Words spelled with OST"},{"start":319.12,"end":322.32,"text":"can be pronounced in two different ways. For example,"},{"start":322.32,"end":323.2,"text":"most,"},{"start":323.2,"end":323.92,"text":"post,"},{"start":323.92,"end":324.88,"text":"and host"},{"start":324.88,"end":330.24,"text":"are pronounced with the O vowel sound. Make sure you say O, it's not aw. It's"},{"start":330.24,"end":332.8,"text":"not mast, it's most."},{"start":332.8,"end":334.08,"text":"post"},{"start":334.08,"end":335.36,"text":"host"},{"start":335.36,"end":336.2,"text":"But,"},{"start":336.2,"end":337.16,"text":"cost,"},{"start":337.16,"end":338.12,"text":"lost,"},{"start":338.12,"end":339.36,"text":"and frost"},{"start":339.36,"end":342.88,"text":"are pronounced with an open sound, an aw sound."},{"start":342.88,"end":344.16,"text":"Cost."},{"start":344.16,"end":346.28,"text":"How much does it cost?"},{"start":346.28,"end":348.72,"text":"I drove to the coast."},{"start":348.72,"end":350.52,"text":"Have you been saying them correctly?"},{"start":350.52,"end":351.8,"text":"Let me know in the comments."},{"start":351.8,"end":353.84,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":353.84,"end":357.92,"text":"Which word has a different vowel sound, or are they the same?"},{"start":357.92,"end":360.24,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":360.24,"end":364.44,"text":"The answer is they're all pronounced with the same vowel sound."},{"start":364.44,"end":365.48,"text":"Listen."},{"start":365.48,"end":366.84,"text":"no"},{"start":366.84,"end":368.16,"text":"road"},{"start":368.16,"end":369.76,"text":"flow"},{"start":369.76,"end":371.28,"text":"old"},{"start":371.28,"end":374.76,"text":"Make sure that you're not saying aw. It's not naw."},{"start":374.76,"end":376.28,"text":"It's no."},{"start":376.28,"end":377.28,"text":"No."},{"start":377.28,"end":378.76,"text":"Oh, no."},{"start":378.76,"end":380.16,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":380.16,"end":381.28,"text":"Oh, no."},{"start":381.28,"end":384.16,"text":"Don't go home."},{"start":384.16,"end":390.8,"text":"Okay, let's go on to the next one. Which vowel sound is different?"},{"start":390.8,"end":392.84,"text":"The third one, fill."},{"start":392.84,"end":394.04,"text":"Listen."},{"start":394.04,"end":395.64,"text":"weak"},{"start":395.64,"end":396.84,"text":"week"},{"start":396.84,"end":398.52,"text":"Exact same pronunciation."},{"start":398.52,"end":400.64,"text":"Those two are homophones."},{"start":400.64,"end":401.84,"text":"fill"},{"start":401.84,"end":404.0,"text":"and seen"},{"start":404.0,"end":407.4,"text":"The third one, fill, is a neutral vowel sound."},{"start":407.4,"end":411.84,"text":"Your lips should be relaxed and your tongue is also relaxed in the back."},{"start":411.84,"end":414.04,"text":"Ih. Ih. Fill."},{"start":414.04,"end":414.84,"text":"Fill."},{"start":414.84,"end":416.96,"text":"Let's say these two words."},{"start":416.96,"end":418.56,"text":"feel"},{"start":418.56,"end":420.6,"text":"fill"},{"start":420.6,"end":422.16,"text":"leave"},{"start":422.16,"end":423.72,"text":"live"},{"start":423.72,"end":425.56,"text":"Have you been pronouncing them correctly?"},{"start":425.56,"end":427.32,"text":"Let's go on to the next one."},{"start":427.32,"end":430.92,"text":"Which vowel sound is different in these four words?"},{"start":430.92,"end":433.72,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":433.72,"end":436.0,"text":"The correct answer is the same."},{"start":436.0,"end":438.96,"text":"They're all pronounced the same. Listen."},{"start":438.96,"end":440.4,"text":"fun"},{"start":440.4,"end":442.0,"text":"sun"},{"start":442.0,"end":443.6,"text":"come"},{"start":443.6,"end":444.92,"text":"up"},{"start":444.92,"end":447.0,"text":"is the neutral uh sound."},{"start":447.0,"end":448.48,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":448.48,"end":452.44,"text":"My son had fun."},{"start":452.44,"end":455.4,"text":"It didn't come up."},{"start":455.4,"end":459.76,"text":"Let's go on to the next one. Let's look at these four words. Which vowel sound"},{"start":459.76,"end":462.76,"text":"is different, or are they all the same?"},{"start":462.76,"end":467.16,"text":"You say them."},{"start":467.16,"end":468.8,"text":"They're all the same."},{"start":468.8,"end":469.84,"text":"Listen."},{"start":469.84,"end":471.16,"text":"mother"},{"start":471.16,"end":472.68,"text":"done"},{"start":472.68,"end":474.2,"text":"tongue"},{"start":474.2,"end":475.12,"text":"country."},{"start":475.12,"end":478.92,"text":"The o u in country is pronounced as an uh"},{"start":478.92,"end":483.48,"text":"uh. I've heard a lot of people mispronounce this word, so make sure you're saying it"},{"start":483.48,"end":484.56,"text":"correctly."},{"start":484.56,"end":485.76,"text":"country"},{"start":485.76,"end":486.68,"text":"country."},{"start":486.68,"end":488.12,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":488.12,"end":489.2,"text":"What country"},{"start":489.2,"end":491.96,"text":"are you from?"},{"start":491.96,"end":496.56,"text":"And from is also pronounced with that vowel sound, the uh sound."},{"start":496.56,"end":498.12,"text":"Let's say it again."},{"start":498.12,"end":500.76,"text":"What country are you from?"},{"start":500.76,"end":502.52,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":502.52,"end":507.24,"text":"Which vowel sound is different in these words, or are all of the vowel sounds the"},{"start":507.24,"end":508.04,"text":"same?"},{"start":508.04,"end":513.36,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":513.36,"end":516.24,"text":"The second one is different. ball"},{"start":516.24,"end":518.76,"text":"Listen to the pronunciation of all four."},{"start":518.76,"end":520.12,"text":"most"},{"start":520.12,"end":521.56,"text":"ball"},{"start":521.56,"end":523.04,"text":"roll"},{"start":523.04,"end":524.32,"text":"own"},{"start":524.32,"end":526.48,"text":"Be careful about these two words."},{"start":526.48,"end":527.64,"text":"ball"},{"start":527.64,"end":528.8,"text":"bowl"},{"start":528.8,"end":534.68,"text":"In American English, the ah in ball is different from British English. In British English, the"},{"start":534.68,"end":536.92,"text":"vowel sound is more rounded."},{"start":536.92,"end":537.88,"text":"Listen."},{"start":537.88,"end":539.08,"text":"ball"},{"start":539.08,"end":540.44,"text":"bowl"},{"start":540.44,"end":542.28,"text":"The vowel sounds are different."},{"start":542.28,"end":544.4,"text":"Let's go on to the next question."},{"start":544.4,"end":548.08,"text":"Which vowel sound is pronounced differently in these words?"},{"start":548.08,"end":550.52,"text":"Or are they the same?"},{"start":550.52,"end":555.12,"text":"You say them."},{"start":555.12,"end":556.72,"text":"The first one is different."},{"start":556.72,"end":558.0,"text":"bought"},{"start":558.0,"end":559.52,"text":"Listen to all four."},{"start":559.52,"end":560.64,"text":"bought"},{"start":560.64,"end":561.76,"text":"boat"},{"start":561.76,"end":563.04,"text":"bowl"},{"start":563.04,"end":564.68,"text":"low"},{"start":564.68,"end":570.8,"text":"In American English, the ah of bought is a bigger vowel sound than in British English."},{"start":570.8,"end":571.8,"text":"Listen."},{"start":571.8,"end":573.24,"text":"bought"},{"start":573.24,"end":574.44,"text":"boat"},{"start":574.44,"end":575.88,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":575.88,"end":578.68,"text":"I bought a new boat."},{"start":578.68,"end":583.52,"text":"Let's go on to the next one. Which vowel sound is pronounced differently in these four"},{"start":583.52,"end":584.28,"text":"words,"},{"start":584.28,"end":586.2,"text":"or are they all the same?"},{"start":586.2,"end":592.2,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":592.2,"end":593.8,"text":"The first one is different."},{"start":593.8,"end":594.76,"text":"Listen."},{"start":594.76,"end":596.08,"text":"though"},{"start":596.08,"end":597.36,"text":"thought"},{"start":597.36,"end":598.84,"text":"cough"},{"start":598.84,"end":600.68,"text":"caught"},{"start":600.68,"end":604.2,"text":"When we add a T, the vowel sound changes."},{"start":604.2,"end":605.6,"text":"though"},{"start":605.6,"end":607.88,"text":"thought"},{"start":607.88,"end":609.64,"text":"Let's go on to the next one."},{"start":609.64,"end":613.08,"text":"Which vowel sound is pronounced differently in these four words,"},{"start":613.08,"end":619.16,"text":"you say them."},{"start":619.16,"end":620.72,"text":"The second one is different."},{"start":620.72,"end":621.8,"text":"Listen."},{"start":621.8,"end":623.12,"text":"were"},{"start":623.12,"end":624.6,"text":"where"},{"start":624.6,"end":626.0,"text":"work"},{"start":626.0,"end":627.92,"text":"girl"},{"start":627.92,"end":629.24,"text":"Repeat after me."},{"start":629.24,"end":633.32,"text":"Where were the girls?"},{"start":633.32,"end":636.44,"text":"Where were the girls?"},{"start":636.44,"end":638.28,"text":"Let's go on to the next one."},{"start":638.28,"end":640.84,"text":"Which vowel sound is pronounced differently"},{"start":640.84,"end":642.36,"text":"in these four words,"},{"start":642.36,"end":644.64,"text":"or are they all pronounced the same?"},{"start":644.64,"end":647.72,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":647.72,"end":652.36,"text":"It depends. Are we talking about American English or British English pronunciation?"},{"start":652.36,"end":657.96,"text":"In American English, all four words are pronounced with the same vowel sound. Listen."},{"start":657.96,"end":659.4,"text":"This"},{"start":659.4,"end":661.16,"text":"sit"},{"start":661.16,"end":662.76,"text":"did"},{"start":662.76,"end":664.24,"text":"been"},{"start":664.24,"end":666.16,"text":"That last one is tricky."},{"start":666.16,"end":667.68,"text":"In American English"},{"start":667.68,"end":668.6,"text":"been"},{"start":668.6,"end":671.68,"text":"and been are pronounced exactly the same."},{"start":671.68,"end":675.72,"text":"But in British English, this word is pronounced as bean."},{"start":675.72,"end":679.44,"text":"British speakers would say, \"Where have you been?\""},{"start":679.44,"end":683.08,"text":"American speakers would say, \"Where have you been?\""},{"start":683.08,"end":686.72,"text":"Let's listen to some native speakers of American English pronouncing"},{"start":686.72,"end":687.52,"text":"been"},{"start":687.52,"end":692.6,"text":"and British English pronouncing it as bean. >> I mean, it's like, \"Where have you been?\" >> I've"},{"start":692.6,"end":697.36,"text":"missed you so much. How have you been? >> How has it been being back in university?"},{"start":697.36,"end":702.28,"text":">> Where have you been the last 10 years? >> How are you? Or how have you been?"},{"start":702.28,"end":704.4,"text":">> How have you been involved?"},{"start":704.4,"end":706.04,"text":">> Let's look at the next question."},{"start":706.04,"end":708.64,"text":"Which vowel sound is pronounced differently?"},{"start":708.64,"end":712.56,"text":"You say them first."},{"start":712.56,"end":714.88,"text":"The correct answer is comb."},{"start":714.88,"end":720.0,"text":"The other three are pronounced the same. Did you know that? Listen."},{"start":720.0,"end":721.56,"text":">> room"},{"start":721.56,"end":723.16,"text":"tomb"},{"start":723.16,"end":724.8,"text":"comb"},{"start":724.8,"end":726.28,"text":"suit"},{"start":726.28,"end":728.04,"text":"So, tomb"},{"start":728.04,"end":729.08,"text":"and comb"},{"start":729.08,"end":731.96,"text":"are spelled similarly, but they're pronounced differently."},{"start":731.96,"end":737.08,"text":"One is pronounced with an ooh, one is pronounced with an o. And in American English,"},{"start":737.08,"end":740.24,"text":"suit has the same vowel sound as room."},{"start":740.24,"end":741.0,"text":"Suit."},{"start":741.0,"end":743.76,"text":"In British English, it's suit."},{"start":743.76,"end":746.24,"text":"Let's say them again. Repeat after me."},{"start":746.24,"end":747.92,"text":"room"},{"start":747.92,"end":749.32,"text":"tomb"},{"start":749.32,"end":750.8,"text":"comb"},{"start":750.8,"end":751.64,"text":"suit."},{"start":751.64,"end":754.68,"text":"If you would like to continue improving your pronunciation"},{"start":754.68,"end":757.28,"text":"and truly master the American accent,"},{"start":757.28,"end":761.84,"text":"I have two options for you. The first option is my self-study"},{"start":761.84,"end":762.56,"text":"course,"},{"start":762.56,"end":765.68,"text":"The American Accent Course. It's a comprehensive"},{"start":765.68,"end":766.6,"text":"step-by-step"},{"start":766.6,"end":767.44,"text":"program"},{"start":767.44,"end":771.2,"text":"that teaches you all the rules of American pronunciation,"},{"start":771.2,"end":772.76,"text":"including vowels,"},{"start":772.76,"end":773.72,"text":"consonants,"},{"start":773.72,"end":774.48,"text":"rhythm,"},{"start":774.48,"end":775.72,"text":"intonation,"},{"start":775.72,"end":777.4,"text":"and very importantly,"},{"start":777.4,"end":782.68,"text":"natural connected speech. And the second option is Accurate English Pro,"},{"start":782.68,"end":785.36,"text":"where in addition to following the lessons,"},{"start":785.36,"end":787.4,"text":"you can get weekly personalized"},{"start":787.4,"end":789.36,"text":"feedback on your accent."},{"start":789.36,"end":791.6,"text":"We listen to your audio file,"},{"start":791.6,"end":792.76,"text":"and we respond"},{"start":792.76,"end":793.84,"text":"by audio."},{"start":793.84,"end":795.52,"text":"We point out your mistakes,"},{"start":795.52,"end":799.72,"text":"and we tell you exactly what you need to work on. You will get personalized"},{"start":799.72,"end":805.68,"text":"feedback every week from me or from one of my expert Accurate English instructors."},{"start":805.68,"end":808.36,"text":"Plus, we have regular live calls"},{"start":808.36,"end":810.0,"text":"where we answer your questions"},{"start":810.0,"end":813.76,"text":"and we correct your accent. This is the kind of detailed feedback"},{"start":813.76,"end":817.08,"text":"that many English learners have never received"},{"start":817.08,"end":822.28,"text":"even after speaking English for 10 years or 20 or even 30 years."},{"start":822.28,"end":824.76,"text":"We will help you identify your specific"},{"start":824.76,"end":825.6,"text":"pronunciation"},{"start":825.6,"end":826.6,"text":"challenges"},{"start":826.6,"end":828.12,"text":"so that you can know exactly"},{"start":828.12,"end":830.0,"text":"what you're doing incorrectly"},{"start":830.0,"end":834.12,"text":"and you will know how to correct them. To learn more, go to the description of"},{"start":834.12,"end":836.68,"text":"this video and check out those links."},{"start":836.68,"end":838.68,"text":"Thanks for watching and keep practicing."}]}